## 4. Automated SiteGround Git-to-SSH deployment

Deployments to SiteGround should use a restricted SSH deploy key in GitHub Actions **when Matt chooses SSH over the existing zip/FTP workflow**. Theme destination is `wp-content/themes/matthummel/`, not `sage-bespoke`.

Reference layout (do not drop this in as a second competing production workflow without Matt’s go-ahead):

```yaml
# .github/workflows/deploy-production.yml
name: Deploy Bespoke Theme to SiteGround Production

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  build-and-deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Checkout Repository Source
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup PHP Environment
        uses: shivammathur/setup-php@v2
        with:
          php-version: '8.3'

      - name: Install Composer Server-side Dependencies
        run: |
          composer install --no-ansi --no-dev --no-interaction --no-plugins --no-progress --no-scripts --optimize-autoloader

      - name: Setup Node.js Build Toolchain
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '22'
          cache: 'npm'

      - name: Build Production Compiled Frontend Assets
        run: |
          npm ci
          npm run build

      - name: Configure Secure SSH Deployment Key
        run: |
          mkdir -p ~/.ssh
          echo "${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_SSH_PRIVATE_KEY }}" > ~/.ssh/id_rsa
          chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_rsa
          ssh-keyscan -p ${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_PORT }} ${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_HOST }} >> ~/.ssh/known_hosts

      - name: Deploy Assets Directly via Rsync Pipeline
        run: |
          rsync -avz -e "ssh -p ${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_PORT }}" \
            --exclude='.git*' \
            --exclude='node_modules' \
            --exclude='tests' \
            ./ ${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_USER }}@${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_HOST }}:/home/customer/www/${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_DOMAIN }}/public_html/wp-content/themes/matthummel/

      - name: Flush Object Caches Remotely via SiteGround SSH
        run: |
          ssh -p ${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_PORT }} ${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_USER }}@${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_HOST }} << 'EOF'
            cd /home/customer/www/${{ secrets.SITEGROUND_DOMAIN }}/public_html/
            wp cache flush
          EOF
```

Private keys live in GitHub Secrets or `.deploy-keys/` locally (gitignored). Public key goes to SiteGround **Site Tools → Devs → SSH Manager**.

